338
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:10,720
padding before performing the

339
00:13:08,399 --> 00:13:12,720
convolution. That's the key difference

340
00:13:10,720 --> 00:13:14,560
between the clean linear convolution

341
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:18,279
result and the wrapped around circular

342
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:18,279
convolution result.

343
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:24,000
Now, let's see how zero padding helps us

344
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:26,399
fix the edge effect problem we saw with

345
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:28,240
circular convolution.

346
00:13:26,399 --> 00:13:30,480
In the earlier example, the red and

347
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:32,720
green lines representing the start and

348
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:35,120
end of the main region we care about

349
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:37,360
were very close together. This caused

350
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:39,760
the signal to wrap around and overlap in

351
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:42,560
places we didn't want.

352
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:44,240
