356
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:53,040
putting some extra space between the

357
00:13:50,480 --> 00:13:54,880
hands. The top and bottom hands are now

358
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:57,760
farther apart before they start

359
00:13:54,880 --> 00:14:00,000
overlapping.

360
00:13:57,760 --> 00:14:02,079
As a result, the main section we care

361
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:04,880
about here, marked in red, remains

362
00:14:02,079 --> 00:14:06,560
untouched by unwanted overlaps. The

363
00:14:04,880 --> 00:14:08,320
green section, which previously had

364
00:14:06,560 --> 00:14:10,000
interference from wrapping, now stays

365
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:11,839
clean.

366
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:13,600
This is exactly how we prevent the

367
00:14:11,839 --> 00:14:16,000
distortion seen in the Wikipedia

368
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:18,399
example. By padding with enough zeros,

369
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:20,560
the circular convolution result becomes

370
00:14:18,399 --> 00:14:23,560
identical to the true linear convolution

371
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:23,560
result.

372
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:30,560
Here's a straightforward mat lab example

373
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:34,399
to show linear convolution in action.

374
00:14:30,560 --> 00:14:39,199
We start with two sequences. X= 5 4 3 2

375
00:14:34,399 --> 00:14:41,199
1 0 H= 1 2 3 4 5 6.

376
00:14:39,199 --> 00:14:43,600
The first figure shows both sequences

377
00:14:41,199 --> 00:14:45,760
plotted together. The blue line is x

378
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:49,519
starting high and decreasing. The red

379
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:51,839
line is h starting low and increasing.

380
00:14:49,519 --> 00:14:53,360
Now we use mat lab's built-in convey

381
00:14:51,839 --> 00:14:57,279
function to compute their linear

382
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:59,040
convolution. Oh, convi equals convex h.

383
00:14:57,279 --> 00:15:02,160
When we plot the result, we see the

384
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:04,399
familiar triangular shape. It rises as

385
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:06,560
the two signals increasingly overlap,

386
00:15:04,399 --> 00:15:10,240
