480
00:18:40,559 --> 00:18:44,960
strong they are. This is incredibly

481
00:18:42,799 --> 00:18:47,280
useful in engineering, science, and even

482
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:49,520
everyday technologies. from analyzing

483
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:51,440
audio signals to detecting features in

484
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:54,880
images to identifying patterns in

485
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:56,640
biomedical data.

486
00:18:54,880 --> 00:18:58,400
In the upcoming slides, we'll take an

487
00:18:56,640 --> 00:19:00,559
example signal, examine its spectrum,

488
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:02,640
and then see how techniques like zero

489
00:19:00,559 --> 00:19:04,559
